ios_integration_patches:
  - custom transport failure preserves resp.transport_retryable
  - retained persistent auth failures no longer publish a premature terminal callback
  - retryable persistent batches reschedule bounded live-process retry cycles with jittered backoff
  - close/destroy promotes and releases delayed persistent retry tasks while leaving WAL unacknowledged for recovery
  - package-internal Core/LZ4 visibility for final Mach-O symbol hiding
  - POSIX persistent file opens use O_NOFOLLOW/O_CLOEXEC when available
  - Bridge config writes effective retry_policy.max_attempts and legacy mirror
  - NSURLSession transport, structured errors, persistence lock/attributes, autorelease pools
  - server-controlled request IDs are bounded/normalized and logs emit fingerprints only
  - official x-tls-requestid response header plus legacy x-tls-request-id compatibility
  - nil STS rotation clears the previous token and header-bound CR/LF is rejected
  - NSURLSession response bodies are capped at 64 KiB and oversize is non-retryable
  - Bridge enforces exact 32-lowercase-hex hash keys and a 9.5 MiB raw batch ceiling
  - persistent post-WAL admission directly merges the encoded builder while preserving contiguous acknowledgement ranges
  - persistent WAL CRC32 uses a format-compatible table lookup and each producer retains at most one reusable idle single-log builder
  - zero is the runtime thread auto-tune sentinel; positive send/pack thread counts, including one, are exact
  - zero is the runtime send-queue auto-tune sentinel; positive task capacities, including 1024, are exact
  - sealed batches transfer their builder allocation into the send task; snapshot/export keep copy semantics and allocation failures remain atomic
  - sender completion and idle cleanup retain hash-key queues with a nonempty aggregate builder, preventing persistent acknowledgement holes and stalled WAL reclamation
  - default/per-log/template hash keys use the SLS-compatible half-open range [00000000000000000000000000000000, ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff); the all-f upper bound is rejected before queue/WAL admission
  - explicit protobuf TimeNs is the nanosecond remainder after Time milliseconds and values >= 1,000,000 are rejected before queue/WAL admission and encoding

